# This is for stage 2. Improves readability and seperates dialogue
# Library
if {target} == "book_pink":
	How to read for dummies.
	Gli: What a book.
elif {target} == "book_blue":
	…is when The Guardian blessed us Figures with the ability to graft. This grafting gave us the potential to express ourselves in ways we could have never imagined.
elif {target} == "book_green":
	(The book is extremely worn-out with most of the pages being torn or completely removed. You can make out a couple of sentences on one of the pages.)
	Curiously, some select groups of avians survived the Beige Blizzard, though none have been spotted for over 400 years in and around Archeo. At first the standard procedure when a Figure spotted an organic was to capture and deliver it to the Cathedral of Archeo.
	In the last 50 years however this has changed. Given that the only organics left are the small groups of avians who cause no problems. there is no real need to capture them. The oth…
elif {target} == "book_purple":
	CHAPTER 1 - The first thing a Figure should know when learning how to graft is the element system. It was discovered very quickly that upon grafting, graftables received one of three elements based on the original use of the item.
	These three elements are\: [color=blue]Paper[/color], [color=red]Rock[/color], and [color=green]Scissors[/color]. Even when items don’t seem like they should have a certain element, they will inherit that element's powers anyways, leading to…
	Gli: [color=blue]Paper[/color], [color=red]Rock[/color], and [color=green]Scissors[/color]. There's something about the order of the elements.
elif {target} == "statue_3":
	join statue_1 left
	statue_1: CHAPTER 2 - After having used graftables for an extended amount of time, it should be known how to properly take care of them. When cleaning or repairing graftables, the element – be it [color=green]Scissors[/color], [color=blue]Paper[/color], or [color=red]Rock[/color] – should be taken into account. Using the wrong tools can cause damage to the graftable or injuries to a Figure themselves
	leave statue_1
	join Gli left
	Gli: [color=green]Scissors[/color], [color=blue]Paper[/color] or [color=red]Rock[/color]. Why did he mention it in this order?
elif {target} == "statue_4":
	join statue_1 left
	statue_1: The role of Communicator is one of the most important positions a Figure can ever receive. It is the Communicator's role to converse with The Guardian and pass on any important information citizens of Archeo should know. It is also the Communicator’s task to help the church with managing the city.
	leave statue_1
	join Gli left
	Gli: Communicator... I hardly know her.
elif {target} == "rock":
	if {sequence_step} == 1.0:
		set {sequence_step} = 2.0
		2
		[signal arg="rock_red"]
	elif {sequence_step} == 5.0:
		set {sequence_step} = 6.0
		winner
		[signal arg="rock_red"]
		audio sfx "res://Sounds/SFX/the-sound-of-the-note-do.mp3"
		[signal arg="puzzle2_complete"]
	else:
		set {sequence_step} = 0
		tset
		[signal arg="reset_puzzle"]
elif {target} == "paper":
	if {sequence_step} == 0.0:
		set {sequence_step} = 1.0
		1
		[signal arg="paper_blue"]
	elif {sequence_step} == 4.0:
		set {sequence_step} = 5.0
		5
		[signal arg="paper_blue"]
	else:
		set {sequence_step} = 0
		tsep
		[signal arg="reset_puzzle"]
elif {target} == "scissor":
	if {sequence_step} == 2.0:
		set {sequence_step} = 3.0
		3
		[signal arg="scissor_green"]
	elif {sequence_step} == 3.0:
		set {sequence_step} = 4.0
		4
		[signal arg="scissor_green"]
	else:
		set {sequence_step} = 0.0
		tstscs
		[signal arg="reset_puzzle"]
elif {target} == "churchbro_defeated":
	join statue_1 rightmost
	statue_1: Don't you dare set foot in that church.
	statue_1: The priest is not accepting visitors... Especially not your kind.
elif {target} == "npc3":
	join Gli left
	join skull right
	Gli: Hey, have you seen anything strange today?
	skull: Strange? Everything is strange now.
	Gli: What do you mean by that?
	skull: Just… stay out of the church.
elif {target} == "npc6":
	join statue_1 left
	statue_1: You haven't been changing, have you?
	statue_1: Oh who am I kidding you're not that kind of figure.
	statue_1: Excuse me. I'm talking to my friend here not you.
elif {target} == "npc4":
	join statue_1 left
	statue_1: Never bro, the priest said that to change is to destroy the Guardians image.
	statue_1: Can you not bother me when I'm talking to my friend.
elif {target} == "npc5":
	join "Armless figure" rightmost
	"Armless figure": Your greed is sickening.
	join Gli left
	Gli: Excuse me.
	"Armless figure": I see those grafts you have. When will it be enough for you.
	Gli: My grafts are my own business
	"Armless figure": You're lucky the priest ordered me to leave you alone.
elif {target} == "churchman1":
	join Leo rightmost
	Leo: I wondered when you would come.
	leave Leo
	join Gli left
	Gli: You knew I would come here?
	leave Gli
	join Leo rightmost
	Leo: You've made quite a mess of things, haven't you.
	Leo: Someone who knows what you are. And what you're becoming. The grafts you carry they're not random. They're part of something older.
	leave Leo
	join Gli left
	Gli: What do you mean?
	leave Gli
	join Leo rightmost
	Leo: There's a library in this district. The figures inside hold the answer. Go. See what's there. Then come back to me.
	leave Leo
	join Gli left
	Gli: Why would I do anything you say?
	leave Gli
	The priest stays silent...
if {target} == "library_locked_1":
	join Gli left
	Gli: I don't have time for this. I should go to the stairs first.
if {target} == "library_locked_2":
	join Gli left
	Gli: I should go to the church first.
if {target} == "churchman_postlibrary":
	join Leo rightmost
	join Gli left
	Leo: What do you think happens when there aren't enough grafts for the figures?
	Gli: Thats... I only changed my grafts because strange things were happening. Not because I want to.
	Leo: Then you wouldn't mind giving me your grafts then right?
	Gli: Wait a second. You just want to be in control of the grafts. You don't care about changelings. You just want to be the only one with power.
	Leo: You're more perceptive than I thought. Oh well now I have another reason to take you down. I pray that the Guardian forgives you when I send you there.
if {target} == "npc5_postchurch":
	join "Armless figure" center
	"Armless figure": fuck you
[end_timeline]